hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27634","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, he said: Haddathana al-Mas'udi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a man of the family of Abu Hathmah, from al-Shifa' bint Abd Allah, and she was a woman among the emigrants, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the best deeds, and he said: Faith in Allah, jihad in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, and an accepted hajj."
"27635","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Mahdi, he said: Haddathana Ali ibn Mushir, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from al-Shifa' bint Abd Allah, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon us while I was with Hafsah, and he said to me: Why do you not teach her the ruqyah of the namlah as you taught her writing?"
"27636","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Akhbarana al-Mas'udi, and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, he said: Haddathana al-Mas'udi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a man of the family of Abu Hathmah, from al-Shifa' bint Abd Allah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked which deeds are best. He said: Faith in Allah, jihad in the path of Allah, and an accepted hajj. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: or an accepted hajj."
